course: dictionary
lesson: 7298
title: The pistil
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A flower has many parts, and each one has a job. The pistil is the female part in the middle of a flower. It is made of three parts: the stigma at the top, the style in the middle, and the ovary at the base. Seeds form inside the pistil.
explain: Read the sentence «In its middle are the stamens, which make a fine powder called pollen, and the pistil, which holds tiny eggs called ovules.» The stamens are the male parts, and they make pollen. The pistil is in the middle too, and it holds the ovules. Look at where each word sits in the sentence to find its meaning.
explain: «Pollination happens when pollen gets carried from the stamens to the sticky top of a pistil.» The sticky top is the stigma, so pollen must land there. Then ask: what word would fit here? Try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: The pistil is the female part in the middle of a flower.
fact: The pistil is made of the stigma, the style and the ovary.
fact: The stigma is the sticky top of the pistil, where pollen lands.
fact: The ovary is the swollen bottom part of the pistil, where seeds form.
fact: The pistil is also called the carpel.
exercise: «In its middle are the stamens, which make a fine powder called pollen, and the pistil, which holds tiny eggs called ovules.» What is the pistil? | The sweet liquid that bees drink | The male part that makes pollen | *The female part in the middle of a flower where seeds form | The green leaves under the flower
exercise: «Pollination happens when pollen gets carried to the sticky top of a pistil.» Which part of the pistil is the sticky top? | *stigma | petal | ovary | stamen
exercise: «After fertilisation the ovules become seeds and the flower's ovary, the swollen bottom part of the pistil, grows into a fruit.» Which part of the pistil is the swollen bottom part? | style | stigma | *ovary | pollen
test: Which of these does NOT carry pollen to a pistil? | *a rock | a butterfly | a bee | the wind
test: What is the ovary? | the powder made by the stamens | *the swollen bottom part of the pistil where seeds form | the stalk of the flower | the sticky top of the pistil
exam: «After fertilisation the ovules become seeds, and the ovary grows into what?» | a petal | *a fruit | a root | a leaf
